1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,378
A knife sharpener pedals
to keep his stone spinning.

2
00:00:03,378 --> 00:00:05,657
A child pulls a string to spin a top.

3
00:00:06,057 --> 00:00:09,492
Each one gives a push, and
the push turns into spin.

4
00:00:09,942 --> 00:00:11,377
Aarav watches a potter.

5
00:00:11,377 --> 00:00:15,355
She kicks the heavy wheel a few
times, and it keeps turning for a long

6
00:00:15,355 --> 00:00:16,255
time.

7
00:00:16,195 --> 00:00:18,140
Each kick is a push at the rim.

8
00:00:18,140 --> 00:00:20,298
Where does the work of that kick go?

9
00:00:20,298 --> 00:00:22,149
And how much spin does it buy?

10
00:00:22,649 --> 00:00:25,737
To answer that, we need
the dynamics of rotation.

11
00:00:26,337 --> 00:00:30,656
Push a cart, and three things
matter: force, mass and acceleration.

12
00:00:31,006 --> 00:00:33,485
A turning wheel has a partner for each.

13
00:00:33,485 --> 00:00:35,391
Torque does the job of force.

14
00:00:35,791 --> 00:00:40,310
Moment of inertia does the job of
mass: how hard the body is to spin.

15
00:00:40,710 --> 00:00:46,033
Angular acceleration does the job of
acceleration: how fast the spin grows.

16
00:00:46,633 --> 00:00:48,015
Our motion notebook.

17
00:00:48,015 --> 00:00:50,113
A heavy wheel on a fixed axle.

18
00:00:50,113 --> 00:00:53,438
Its moment of inertia is
four kilogram metre squared.

19
00:00:53,788 --> 00:00:58,006
The foot pushes the rim with twenty
newtons, half a metre from the axle.

20
00:00:58,006 --> 00:01:00,754
Torque: twenty times
half, ten newton metres.

21
00:01:01,154 --> 00:01:02,515
Watch it spin up.

22
00:01:02,515 --> 00:01:04,241
Alpha is torque over I.

23
00:01:04,241 --> 00:01:05,388
Ten over four.

24
00:01:05,388 --> 00:01:08,201
Two point five radians per second squared.

25
00:01:08,601 --> 00:01:11,004
After two seconds, the push stops.

26
00:01:11,004 --> 00:01:15,722
The wheel has turned five radians,
and spins at five radians per second.

27
00:01:16,222 --> 00:01:17,561
The push is gone.

28
00:01:17,561 --> 00:01:20,598
Will the wheel slow
down, or keep its spin?

29
00:01:20,598 --> 00:01:21,767
Ignore friction.

30
00:01:21,767 --> 00:01:23,045
Pause and decide.

31
00:01:26,145 --> 00:01:27,585
It keeps its spin!

32
00:01:27,585 --> 00:01:30,070
No torque, no angular acceleration.

33
00:01:30,070 --> 00:01:32,627
It stays at five radians per second.

34
00:01:33,127 --> 00:01:34,047
Slow-mo replay.

35
00:01:34,047 --> 00:01:36,041
Freeze in the middle of the push.

36
00:01:36,391 --> 00:01:41,714
In a tiny turn, d theta, the rim
moves a small arc, r times d theta.

37
00:01:42,114 --> 00:01:44,185
The force acts along that arc.

38
00:01:44,185 --> 00:01:46,226
So the work is F r d theta.

39
00:01:46,226 --> 00:01:48,247
That is torque times d theta.

40
00:01:48,647 --> 00:01:52,340
On the graph, energy grows in
a straight line with angle.

41
00:01:52,340 --> 00:01:55,439
The slope is the torque,
ten joules per radian.

42
00:01:55,839 --> 00:01:57,956
Fifty joules of work went in.

43
00:01:57,956 --> 00:02:01,705
The wheel now holds exactly
fifty joules of spin energy.

44
00:02:02,305 --> 00:02:05,477
But why does a spinning
wheel have kinetic energy?

45
00:02:05,477 --> 00:02:06,518
Link by link.

46
00:02:06,868 --> 00:02:09,620
Every bit of the wheel moves in a circle.

47
00:02:09,620 --> 00:02:12,178
A bit at distance r moves at r omega.

48
00:02:12,578 --> 00:02:18,004
Its energy is one half m v squared,
so one half m r squared omega squared.

49
00:02:18,404 --> 00:02:19,765
Add all the bits.

50
00:02:19,765 --> 00:02:21,929
The sum of m r squared is I.

51
00:02:21,929 --> 00:02:25,179
So the spin energy is
one half I omega squared.

52
00:02:25,779 --> 00:02:28,225
Now the rules, one step at a time.

53
00:02:28,575 --> 00:02:29,516
Step one.

54
00:02:29,516 --> 00:02:31,294
Work in a tiny turn.

55
00:02:31,294 --> 00:02:35,102
d W equals F r d theta,
which is tau d theta.

56
00:02:35,852 --> 00:02:36,752
Step two.

57
00:02:36,714 --> 00:02:39,913
For a steady torque,
add up the tiny turns.

58
00:02:39,913 --> 00:02:41,428
W equals tau theta.

59
00:02:42,178 --> 00:02:43,098
Step three.

60
00:02:43,098 --> 00:02:44,900
Work per second is power.

61
00:02:44,900 --> 00:02:46,341
P equals tau omega.

62
00:02:47,091 --> 00:02:47,991
Step four.

63
00:02:47,984 --> 00:02:50,305
This power feeds the spin energy.

64
00:02:50,305 --> 00:02:52,524
Tau omega equals I omega alpha.

65
00:02:53,274 --> 00:02:54,174
Step five.

66
00:02:54,111 --> 00:02:55,093
Cancel omega.

67
00:02:55,093 --> 00:02:56,479
Tau equals I alpha.

68
00:02:56,479 --> 00:02:58,645
Newton's second law, for turning.

69
00:02:59,395 --> 00:03:00,295
Remember this.

70
00:03:00,281 --> 00:03:03,947
A torque does work as it turns,
and that work becomes spin energy.

71
00:03:04,647 --> 00:03:05,756
Side by side.

72
00:03:05,756 --> 00:03:10,133
The same torque, ten newton
metres, over the same five radians.

73
00:03:10,533 --> 00:03:12,854
A light wheel, with I equal to one.

74
00:03:12,854 --> 00:03:15,454
And a heavy wheel, with I equal to four.

75
00:03:16,054 --> 00:03:17,021
Now you try.

76
00:03:17,021 --> 00:03:19,678
Which wheel ends up with more spin energy?

77
00:03:19,678 --> 00:03:20,880
Pause and decide.

78
00:03:24,080 --> 00:03:24,980
The same!

79
00:03:24,853 --> 00:03:28,633
Both get fifty joules: the
work, tau theta, is the same.

80
00:03:28,633 --> 00:03:30,810
The light wheel just spins faster.

81
00:03:31,460 --> 00:03:33,150
Now, one worked example.

82
00:03:33,500 --> 00:03:38,393
A motor spins a grinding wheel, I
equal to zero point five, from rest to

83
00:03:38,393 --> 00:03:41,247
twenty radians per second in four seconds.

84
00:03:41,247 --> 00:03:43,832
Find torque, work and average power.

85
00:03:44,332 --> 00:03:47,155
Angular acceleration is twenty over four.

86
00:03:47,155 --> 00:03:49,436
Five radians per second squared.

87
00:03:50,186 --> 00:03:51,671
Torque is I alpha.

88
00:03:51,671 --> 00:03:53,701
Zero point five times five.

89
00:03:53,701 --> 00:03:55,838
Two point five newton metres.

90
00:03:56,588 --> 00:03:58,961
Work equals the spin energy gained.

91
00:03:58,961 --> 00:04:02,671
One half, times zero point
five, times twenty squared.

92
00:04:02,671 --> 00:04:04,058
One hundred joules.

93
00:04:04,808 --> 00:04:07,343
Average power: one hundred over four.

94
00:04:07,343 --> 00:04:08,660
Twenty five watts.

95
00:04:09,310 --> 00:04:10,772
Now, the exam trap.

96
00:04:11,122 --> 00:04:15,912
Many students put omega in r p m
straight into one half I omega squared.

97
00:04:16,312 --> 00:04:19,422
But omega must be in radians per second.

98
00:04:19,422 --> 00:04:24,673
One hundred and twenty r p m is one
hundred and twenty times two pi over

99
00:04:24,673 --> 00:04:26,131
sixty: four pi.

100
00:04:26,781 --> 00:04:28,068
Where is this asked?

101
00:04:28,068 --> 00:04:31,386
In torque and work, power,
and flywheel energy questions.

102
00:04:31,986 --> 00:04:33,281
Exam level now.

103
00:04:33,281 --> 00:04:38,320
A flywheel with I equal to two kilogram
metre squared spins at six hundred

104
00:04:38,320 --> 00:04:39,220
r p m.

105
00:04:39,122 --> 00:04:42,284
A steady brake stops
it in ten revolutions.

106
00:04:42,284 --> 00:04:44,139
Find the braking torque.

107
00:04:44,139 --> 00:04:45,490
Pause and solve.

108
00:04:50,890 --> 00:04:52,358
The answer is B.

109
00:04:52,358 --> 00:04:54,281
Twenty pi newton metres.

110
00:04:54,781 --> 00:04:57,898
Omega: six hundred
times two pi over sixty.

111
00:04:57,898 --> 00:04:59,989
Twenty pi radians per second.

112
00:05:00,489 --> 00:05:04,373
Spin energy: one half times
two times twenty pi squared.

113
00:05:04,373 --> 00:05:06,549
Four hundred pi squared joules.

114
00:05:07,049 --> 00:05:09,649
Ten revolutions is twenty pi radians.

115
00:05:09,649 --> 00:05:13,338
Torque times twenty pi equals
four hundred pi squared.

116
00:05:13,338 --> 00:05:16,002
So torque is twenty pi newton metres.

117
00:05:16,602 --> 00:05:18,143
Here is your recap.

118
00:05:18,143 --> 00:05:19,726
Screenshot this card.

119
00:05:22,926 --> 00:05:24,865
Can you answer these without help?

120
00:05:25,265 --> 00:05:26,165
One.

121
00:05:25,692 --> 00:05:28,665
Why does the wheel keep
spinning after the push stops?

122
00:05:29,565 --> 00:05:30,465
Two.

123
00:05:29,994 --> 00:05:33,832
Why do a light and a heavy wheel get
the same spin energy from the same

124
00:05:33,832 --> 00:05:34,732
push?

125
00:05:35,203 --> 00:05:36,103
Three.

126
00:05:35,786 --> 00:05:40,072
Why must omega be in radians per
second in one half I omega squared?

127
00:05:40,972 --> 00:05:44,232
Next time: spin on a chair
and pull your arms in.

128
00:05:44,232 --> 00:05:46,654
Nobody pushes you, yet you speed up.

129
00:05:46,654 --> 00:05:47,554
How?

130
00:05:47,134 --> 00:05:49,151
Conservation of angular momentum.
